      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "When the value of this property is [`true`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/true), the animator remains in the [`UIViewAnimatingState.active`](uiviewanimatingstate/active.md) state when the animation finishes, and it does not execute its completion handler.",
      "normalizedSource": "When the value of this property is [`true`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/true), the animator remains in the [`UIViewAnimatingState.active`](uiviewanimatingstate/active.md) state when the animation finishes, and it does not execute its completion handler.",
      "sourceHash": "15679da889f20d7b338f4d3670300b2854d646f7be3b72f3e39e18be82902ada",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "Keeping the animator in the [`UIViewAnimatingState.active`](uiviewanimatingstate/active.md) state allows you to reverse the animation even after it has finished.",
      "documentTitle": "pausesOnCompletion",
      "framework": "UIKit",
      "ko": "",
